  "notes": "FORMS:\n{会|かい} (meet) + {談|だん} (talk, discuss)\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed for formal discussions between leaders, officials, or representatives — typically in diplomatic or political contexts. Implies greater formality and importance than ordinary {会議|かいぎ} (meeting).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {首脳|しゅのう}{会談|かいだん}: summit meeting\n- {日米|にちべい}{会談|かいだん}: Japan-US talks\n- {電話|でんわ}{会談|かいだん}: telephone conference\n- {会談|かいだん}を{行|おこな}う: to hold talks\n- {会談|かいだん}を{申|もう}し{入|い}れる: to request a meeting\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {会議|かいぎ}: meeting (general, any participants)\n- {会談|かいだん}: talks (formal, usually leaders/officials)\n- {対談|たいだん}: dialogue, interview (often published or broadcast)\n- {面談|めんだん}: interview, private meeting (often one-on-one)",
